1
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:18,226
[sighs] I can't believe he's gone.

2
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,189
I don't think I can go back
to that empty house,

3
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:24,066
open the door and...

4
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:29,571
not hear his nails scratching on the floor
as he runs to it.

5
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:32,532
You know what? I'm gonna...
I'll meet you there.

6
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:35,327
Okay.

7
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:55,972
-[chuckles softly] This is a nice place.
-Thank you.

8
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:01,853
You moved on up.

9
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:04,939
Why couldn't you have lived here
when we were together?

10
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:06,066
What are you saying? You...

11
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:08,693
you didn't enjoy
the cramped studio apartment

12
00:01:08,776 --> 00:01:10,737
-in the Valley with no air conditioning?
-[chuckles]

13
00:01:12,905 --> 00:01:15,492
[sighs] This is harder than I thought.

14
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:18,536
Think about it this way...

15
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:21,206
This is the first time you have to
come home without him here.

16
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,750
It's never gonna be as bad as this.

17
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:27,170
That's actually not necessarily true.

18
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:33,050
When my dad died,
it actually got harder as time went on.

19
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:36,179
-Oh.
-Sorry. I know you're trying to help.

20
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:40,975
Do you remember when he used to lie
on the floor and watch us have sex?

21
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:46,814
-That, uh, creeped you out, as I recall.
-Mmm-hmm. Yeah.

22
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:49,066
It was another set of eyes
watching me have sex.

23
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:51,861
-He didn't know what he was seeing.
-He absolutely did.

24
00:01:51,944 --> 00:01:53,238
[laughs]

25
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:55,990
I think he even knew
when it was make-up sex.

26
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:57,409
Hmm.

27
00:01:59,076 --> 00:02:00,912
I kinda feel like, um...

28
00:02:01,829 --> 00:02:05,875
our entire relationship
was just amazing make-up sex.

29
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:07,418
Yeah.

30
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:09,629
Yeah.

31
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,435
[theme music playing]

32
00:02:39,451 --> 00:02:40,952
-Morning, Sam.
-Hi, Gus.

33
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,082
[sighs]

34
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:54,549
[Victor speaking Korean]

35
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:56,008
[Tommy] Mmm-hmm.

36
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,594
-Hello!
-[speaking Korean]

37
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:59,178
-Hey! Good--
-Oh.

38
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:01,598
Hey, Gus, uh, we're actually
kind of busy right now. So...

39
00:03:01,681 --> 00:03:04,517
Oh, yeah, no, I won't...
I won't take up much of your time.

40
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,353
Guys, I just, um...

41
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:10,648
Hey, I just wanted to say I'm sorry
for how things kinda got ugly there.

42
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:14,819
And I just also wanted to say
thank you so much

43
00:03:14,902 --> 00:03:18,197
for listening to my ideas
on the Arctic movie.

44
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:23,328
So, um, just wanted to give you this, uh,
map of the North Pole...

45
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:25,413
-Wow! [laughs]
-just in case it inspires anything

46
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:27,540
for your movie. And then, uh,

47
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:32,337
when you finally get that movie green-lit,
here's a bottle of soju to celebrate.

48
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,464
-[speaking Korean and laughing]
-Yeah.

49
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:37,174
-[speaking Korean]
-Hey, all right!

50
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:38,260
-[chuckles]
-Thank you.

51
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:40,262
-Yeah, thanks so much.
-Yeah, of course.

52
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:43,097
-Very thoughtful of you.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah, happy to.

53
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:44,224
-Very happy to.
-Thank you.

54
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,976
-Uh, we're gonna get back to work here.
-Yeah. Yeah, get back to it.

55
00:03:47,059 --> 00:03:50,187
-[speaking Korean]
-Hmm.

56
00:03:54,942 --> 00:03:56,278
-[Tommy] Mmm-hmm.
-That's cool.

57
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,446
-[Victor speaking Korean]
-Yeah...

58
00:03:58,530 --> 00:03:59,656
What's going on, Gus?

59
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:02,450
Oh, nothing. Before I go,
I just wanted to let you know

60
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:05,287
I was actually able to rejigger some
of my schedule,

61
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,081
and I think I'll be able
to go to New York now.

62
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:13,002
So, you know, if you wanted me to come
and kick around ideas, I can. So...

63
00:04:13,085 --> 00:04:16,213
Gus, the ship has sailed.
I mean, for Victor it's important

64
00:04:16,298 --> 00:04:19,050
that people be into a project
from the get-go, so...

65
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,636
-Oh.
-[speaking Korean]

66
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:24,221
[stammers]
We really need to get back to work, so...

67
00:04:24,972 --> 00:04:27,309
All right, well,
I'll let you guys go, and, uh...

68
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:30,603
Or I'll let you get back to work,
and, um... Yeah.

69
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:36,943
[sighs]

70
00:04:43,115 --> 00:04:45,410
Come on, let's not bite the nails.
Not a good look.

71
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:48,120
[chuckling] Uh, sorry.
Nervous habit, I guess.

72
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:49,747
Been a rough day?

73
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,583
All right.

74
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:55,670
-Wanna hang out tonight?
-Seriously?

75
00:04:56,588 --> 00:04:57,589
Yeah.

76
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:00,091
Let's get some beers or something.

77
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:02,259
Arya goes to bed at 9:00.

78
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:04,053
I'm bored out of my fucking brains

79
00:05:04,136 --> 00:05:07,306
and I can't watch Dateline anymore
in that hotel room.

80
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:08,475
Yeah, no, that'd be awesome.

81
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:10,560
I could actually use the company.
That'd be nice.

82
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:12,395
-Your place.
-Yeah, my place.

83
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:13,771
-Sure.
-Awesome.

84
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:17,024
-All right. I might bring a friend.
-What's that?

85
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:20,528
-Oh, hey! [chuckles]
-[man] Hey.

86
00:05:20,612 --> 00:05:23,114
-Sorry. Stupid place to sit.
-No worries.

87
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,750
Hey, I'm gonna head out.

88
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,292
Where are you going?
I'm making chilaquiles.

89
00:05:35,377 --> 00:05:38,212
Ugh, I have so much bullshit to do today.

90
00:05:39,381 --> 00:05:40,548
Are we cool?

91
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:41,799
Yeah.

92
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:44,594
Not, uh, weirded out
about the fact that we had sex?

93
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:47,221
-No.
-Good.

94
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,807
Hey, um... [clears throat]

95
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,476
you can tell me
if this is none of my business,

96
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:54,562
but, uh, when I saw you
at the movies the other day,

97
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:58,733
you were obviously with someone.
Is that, like, a serious thing, or...

98
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,860
Um, you know,

99
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,779
we've been seeing each other
for, like, a month.

100
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:06,115
I thought it was gonna get serious,
but then it got really weird.

101
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:09,952
-We never said we were exclusive.
-Good. For your sake.

102
00:06:11,078 --> 00:06:13,456
He was obviously very desperate
for me to like him.

103
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,751
-Ah, he's just from the Midwest.
-Ah! Is that why he's so boring?

104
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:19,003
[both chuckle]

105
00:06:19,086 --> 00:06:20,505
Gotta be careful, Mickey.

106
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:23,049
Boring people are dangerous.
They'll make you boring, too.

107
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:24,634
All right. Can we drop this now?

108
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:26,844
Uh, actually, you guys
didn't even look like a couple.

109
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:30,014
You looked more like a brother-sister
alt-rock band.

110
00:06:30,097 --> 00:06:32,391
-We did not.
-[chuckles] No, no, it was actually worse.

111
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:34,602
You looked like a... a Christian folk duo.

112
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:36,312
All right, I'm gonna go.

113
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:37,980
-[chuckles] Call me later.
-Right.

114
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:45,279
[man] I like the pepper
on that stuff right there.

115
00:06:45,362 --> 00:06:48,240
-[woman speaking indistinctly]
-[boy] A bacon fry.

116
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,492
Ooh, wait, wait, wait.

117
00:06:49,576 --> 00:06:51,661
-[laughs]
-Let me try.

118
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:52,954
[woman] You knew he was gonna do that.

119
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,206
-You knew he was gonna do that.
-[all chuckling]

120
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:56,332
[man] Could be warmer.

121
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:59,210
[boy] We should've ordered
ranch dressing.

122
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:01,754
Dad, can he sit with us?

123
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:04,591
[woman] Aw.

124
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,177
Well, what do you think?

125
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,431
Um, sir?

126
00:07:13,475 --> 00:07:14,851
-Hmm?
-Hi.

127
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:18,813
-Hi.
-Um, would you like to eat with us?

128
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:23,317
Oh, uh... yeah, thanks.

129
00:07:24,318 --> 00:07:27,196
You know what? This is... this is so cool.
This is awesome.

130
00:07:27,279 --> 00:07:28,615
You know, it reminds me of...

131
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:31,075
My dad used to take
my family and I to Denny's.

132
00:07:31,158 --> 00:07:34,537
Oh, and we loved it. We would flip out!

133
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,372
-[laughs]
-I remember, one time...

134
00:07:36,455 --> 00:07:39,166
one time, my mom let us have
Pepsi for breakfast...

135
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,251
[woman] Whoa!

136
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:42,419
which I thought was,
like, the coolest thing.

137
00:07:42,504 --> 00:07:47,424
It's just... it's so cool to be, you know,
with a... with a family...

138
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:52,597
and to, like, just...
like, be around this vibe.

139
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:55,933
'Cause I just, I...

140
00:07:57,184 --> 00:08:02,148
I think... I'm, like, lonely out here,
and I just... I'm feeling homesick.

141
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:09,238
I've never seen such a sad grown-up.

142
00:08:09,321 --> 00:08:11,741
-Can we get the check?
-Oh, this is embarrassing. [chuckles]

143
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:14,035
-Oh, that's okay.
-[exclaims]

144
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:16,954
Man, I don't mean to dump
everything out on you guys or...

145
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,414
-That's fine.
-Don't worry about it.

146
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:19,498
I'll give you my address.

147
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:22,001
You guys can come over and dump
your feelings on me sometime.

148
00:08:22,084 --> 00:08:23,085
[all laughing]

149
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,337
-[cell phone vibrating]
-Oh, hold on. Sorry.

150
00:08:26,255 --> 00:08:29,759
Oh, you know what? I gotta...
I gotta take this.

151
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:32,136
But, um, let me pay for this.

152
00:08:32,219 --> 00:08:33,763
-No! No, no.
-No, no, no, let me pay.

153
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:35,598
Thank you so much for everything.

154
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:38,935
-Hi.
-[Mickey] Hey.

155
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:44,440
-I miss you.
-[Gus] I, uh... I miss you, too.

156
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:47,735
I'm sorry that I got so angry
when we Skyped.

157
00:08:47,819 --> 00:08:50,487
No, no, no, it's okay. I was...

158
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:54,241
I was the one who was acting crazy.
[stammers and chuckles]

159
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,035
It's nice to hear from you.

160
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:59,163
Um... what've you been up to?
How are you doing?

161
00:08:59,246 --> 00:09:02,584
I've been good.
Yeah, work's been really great actually.

162
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:07,296
Uh... I managed to convince that girl
to come over and do a show with us, so...

163
00:09:07,379 --> 00:09:09,591
Oh, no way.
Oh, that's amazing, Mickey.

164
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:13,135
Yeah, so now Erika's
gonna let me kind of run with it.

165
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:16,764
It's gonna be my show, and I can make
the full-time transition from, uh,

166
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:18,808
you know, program manager to producer.

167
00:09:18,891 --> 00:09:22,228
Oh, my gosh, that's great.
Look at you, caring about work.

168
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:24,647
-I'm proud of ya.
-That's a little condescending,

169
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:25,815
but whatever.

170
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:30,444
No, no, I didn't mean it...
that way. Sorry.

171
00:09:30,527 --> 00:09:35,282
It's fine, it's fine.
So, um, what've you been up to?

172
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:38,870
Have you been fucking a bunch
of actresses on the set?

173
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:42,456
What? No, I'm with you.

174
00:09:42,539 --> 00:09:45,584
I... I know that.
I was just... I was kidding.

175
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:46,669
-Oh, yeah.
-Whatever.

176
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:49,631
No, that's... that's funny. Uh...

177
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:55,344
So how's everything else?
Are you... are you doing okay?

178
00:09:55,427 --> 00:09:59,682
You just... You sound like something...
something's going on.

179
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:03,435
-Are you okay?
-What do you mean, something's going on?

180
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:07,064
I don't know. You just sound,
like, upset or manic or...

181
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:10,359
Manic? What? No, I'm not manic.

182
00:10:10,442 --> 00:10:12,444
I didn't know
you were now my psychiatrist, too.

183
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:16,323
I'm fine. Thanks for checking in, Dr. Gus.

184
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:19,786
-I'm just... concerned.
-Don't be concerned, dude!

185
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:22,705
I'm not concerned about you.
[stammers]

186
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:26,918
This is the shit that makes me pull away.

187
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:30,463
[stammers] I shouldn't have called you.
I'm sorry. I gotta go.

188
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:32,799
Okay, Mickey?

189
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:36,177
Shit. Fuck.

190
00:10:36,678 --> 00:10:39,305
[woman] Hi, do you have a few seconds
to help save our oceans?

191
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:42,266
Oh, I'm sorry.
I have ice cream sandwiches.

192
00:10:42,349 --> 00:10:45,394
They melt, and then they're just not
as good when you re-freeze them.

193
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:50,817
You know what? I'd be pretty selfish
if I didn't help the shellfish--

194
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,277
-[Bertie] Oh, my God!
-[woman] Oh, shit!

195
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,829
-[knocking on door]
-[Steven] Hey.

196
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:07,499
-Hey, who is that?
-[Steven] Let me in.

197
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:08,584
Ah!

198
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:09,961
-[both laugh]
-You got me!

199
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:12,379
I mean, I knew it was you,
but, uh, you still got me.

200
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:15,007
-Ooh! Ah!
-Hey, I just, uh,

201
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,094
ordered some chicken fingers,
if you want in on that, yeah?

202
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:20,554
Oh, okay. Knock yourself out.
Let's do it.

203
00:11:20,637 --> 00:11:23,557
Maybe I'll, uh, fire up some Ride Along 2.

204
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,809
Ooh!

205
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:31,983
Hey, listen, um... Good news.
I invited an extra from the set over here.

206
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:34,068
-Oh, okay.
-[grunts]

207
00:11:34,651 --> 00:11:37,780
You know, I think they like
to be called background actors.

208
00:11:37,864 --> 00:11:39,448
I think she likes to be called Natasha.

209
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:42,785
Natasha? Okay, that's cool.

210
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:46,372
I would have invited her to my room,
but, you know, I share it with Arya,

211
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:48,750
-so that's a drag.
-Mmm-hmm. Yeah.

212
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,001
Are you okay? You seem a little off.

213
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,336
Uh, I don't know. I'm all right.

214
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:55,714
Things are a little weird
with Mickey right now. I...

215
00:11:56,548 --> 00:11:59,176
The plane ticket thing
didn't go over well.

216
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,302
-No!
-Yeah,

217
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:04,766
-she's not like the big gestures type.
-No! Oh, shit!

218
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,726
Yikes. All right, well, change of plan.

219
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:09,437
You know what you do now?
Give her some space.

220
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:14,358
Yeah, just keep my distance.
Let her have some room. That makes sense.

221
00:12:14,441 --> 00:12:18,070
Yeah, trust me. She'll be sprinting back
to you once you ice her.

222
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,365
Yeah, well,
that's really my only option that's left.

223
00:12:21,448 --> 00:12:24,952
-But it's hard, man. It's really hard.
-Hey, listen, life is hard.

224
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:27,454
That's what keeps
the Seagram's company in business.

225
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:28,747
-[both laughing]
-[knocking on door]

226
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:31,208
Oh, oh, oh!
Look who it is. Look who it is.

227
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:32,709
-Do you want to answer it--
-No, you...

228
00:12:32,794 --> 00:12:33,961
Okay.

229
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:37,298
-[all] Hi!
-[Gus] Hello.

230
00:12:37,381 --> 00:12:39,591
-Oh, hello.
-Hi, I'm Natasha.

231
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:41,844
-Starlet, welcome to the Oscars.
-Hi!

232
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:45,639
-Ooh, this room is nice.
-Oh, yeah, right?

233
00:12:45,722 --> 00:12:47,641
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-This is Gus.

234
00:12:47,724 --> 00:12:51,478
-Oh, Gus, so you're the one with the...
-The one with the...

235
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:53,397
-[Natasha laughs]
-[Steven] Gettin' right at it.

236
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:56,108
-The... the chicken fingers?
-Wait a second. What do you got back...

237
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:58,069
-The coke! [laughs]
-Yay!

238
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,154
-You're the man, Gus!
-Is that coke?

239
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:01,488
-Oh.
-Yeah.

240
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:05,242
-[dramatic music playing]
-♪ A heart full of love... ♪

241
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:06,327
Hey!

242
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:09,914
Were you here last night?
I didn't hear you come in.

243
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,707
Oh, yeah, I was out super late.

244
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:15,044
Uh, Truman was acting nuts.

245
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:16,795
It's a long, boring story.

246
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:17,880
How are ya?

247
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:22,509
-I almost died today.
-What? Are you okay?

248
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:25,762
A car hit my shopping cart
while I was pushing it.

249
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:28,933
And I saw a grapefruit explode
where my head could've been.

250
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:31,518
This grapefruit. Look at it.

251
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:35,522
-Jesus.
-I was just looking at this grapefruit,

252
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:39,610
and I was thinking...
life could end at any moment

253
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:42,029
and I've settled for so many things.

254
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:47,076
If I had died today, my obituary
would've read, "Survived by Randy."

255
00:13:47,659 --> 00:13:48,660
Shit.

256
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:54,458
-I think I have to end it.
-You're gonna break up with him?

257
00:13:54,541 --> 00:13:57,544
I prefer to think of it
as setting us both free.

258
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:58,670
Here's my advice.

259
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:02,049
Do it over text, and then block his number
so he can't yell at you.

260
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:05,052
No. I owe him the respect
of doing it in person.

261
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:08,555
Maybe I'm naive, but I feel like I could
do it in a way where, at the end of it,

262
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:11,642
-he actually feels better about himself.
-Seriously?

263
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:13,519
Yeah, I've got a knack
for this sort of thing.

264
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:16,022
Once I had to fire someone,
and it took hours,

265
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,191
but we ended up talking about everything,
everything in our lives.

266
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:21,610
-And we still e-mail today.
-About what?

267
00:14:21,693 --> 00:14:25,739
About the fact that I fired him
and he can't get work anymore.

268
00:14:25,822 --> 00:14:27,699
But it's friendly. It's good.

269
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:28,867
[rock music playing]

270
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,870
-[Natasha] Whoo!
-Let's do it.

271
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:35,207
-Hey, Tash, make, uh, Gus another drink.
-Oh, Gus needs another drink.

272
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:38,044
No, I got a couple more sips
left here that I'm--

273
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:40,837
-Oh, I think we can fill it up!
-[Steven] Come on.

274
00:14:40,922 --> 00:14:42,256
-Okay.
-[Natasha chuckles]

275
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:44,800
-Come on, let's turn on some real music.
-[Natasha] Yeah.

276
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,468
-Hey, Gus?
-[Gus] Mmm-hmm?

277
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,804
This little line's got your name on it.

278
00:14:48,887 --> 00:14:50,639
-[dance music playing]
-I haven't eaten dinner.

279
00:14:50,722 --> 00:14:53,642
-[laughs]
-[Steven] Oh, come on, it's Atlanta.

280
00:14:53,725 --> 00:14:55,978
-Yeah, Gus, it's Atlanta. [laughing]
-Oh, well...

281
00:14:56,062 --> 00:14:58,564
I don't know why that matters,
but... [chuckles]

282
00:14:58,647 --> 00:15:00,107
[both] 'Cause it's Atlanta.

283
00:15:00,191 --> 00:15:03,735
[singsong] It's Atlanta! It's Atlanta!
It's Atlanta!

284
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:12,786
-[Natasha] Ooh!
-You guys are having fun.

285
00:15:12,869 --> 00:15:14,663
Uh-oh, here she comes!

286
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,668
We all have to do this.

287
00:15:19,751 --> 00:15:22,713
'Cause if you don't do it,
we'll feel like you're judging us.

288
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:24,924
Yeah, don't judge us, Gus!

289
00:15:26,883 --> 00:15:27,884
Ah!

290
00:15:27,969 --> 00:15:29,971
Ooh! Yes!

291
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,767
[speaking indistinctly]

292
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,979
[babbling]

293
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:41,315
I remember when I was a kid,
my family and I, we would go to church,

294
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:43,234
and I, like, loved Jesus.

295
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:46,570
-That's so sweet.
-Jesus was, like, my best fucking friend,

296
00:15:46,653 --> 00:15:48,990
and I feel like I don't even talk
to Jesus anymore.

297
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:52,326
When was the last time you guys
talked to Jesus? Do you wanna pray?

298
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:54,411
-Uh...
-No fucking way.

299
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:56,330
-Not right now.
-Yeah.

300
00:15:56,413 --> 00:16:00,001
-[Gus] I'm gonna just pray real quick.
-You need another drink.

301
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,086
[coughing]

302
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,214
Hey, we're gonna take off, man!
You good?

303
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:06,507
Okay!

304
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:10,802
-Bye, buddy!
-It was nice to meet you!

305
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:13,305
-[Steven] All right.
-[Gus retching and coughing]

306
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:14,515
Hey!

307
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:15,974
[laughs]

308
00:16:25,692 --> 00:16:26,818
[cell phone chimes]

309
00:16:39,706 --> 00:16:41,000
[knocking on door]

310
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:45,421
Hey!

311
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:47,548
[screaming and clanging over headphones]

312
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,557
-Hi!
-Oh, hey!

313
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,600
-Sorry I scared you.
-[groans]

314
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:01,395
-Whoa! [chuckles]
-That's okay.

315
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:04,648
When I saw you,
I thought you were my neighbor Kelly.

316
00:17:04,731 --> 00:17:07,568
He loves to prank me.
I fucking hate that guy.

317
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:09,528
-Okay.
-What's going on?

318
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:13,657
Um, well, I actually have
some really exciting news for you.

319
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:16,368
Something that's gonna
open up your life in many ways.

320
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:19,538
That sounds great.
What did we, like, win something?

321
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:22,624
We did not.
Um, I'm breaking up with you.

322
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,042
-What?
-Hear me out.

323
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,294
Um, this break up,

324
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:29,090
it's actually gonna give you
a lot of really exciting opportunities

325
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:30,424
to meet new people.

326
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:34,345
It's time for you
to take your wings and soar,

327
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:39,015
because, um, you're ready,
and I can't hold you back.

328
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,267
[toilet flushing]

329
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,146
-Oh, I didn't realize someone was here.
-Oh, hey.

330
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:46,898
Bertie, this is my brother, Devon.
Surprise visit.

331
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:48,359
-Hey.
-Hi.

332
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:50,111
-Uh, sorry, they're wet.
-Very wet.

333
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,612
Oh, they're clean. [chuckles]

334
00:17:51,695 --> 00:17:54,281
-Very wet.
-He, uh... he loves surprises.

335
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:56,617
-I hate surprises.
-Since he was a kid.

336
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,203
Oh, Bertie, it is so cool
to finally meet you,

337
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:01,288
'cause this guy
won't stop talking about you

338
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:04,333
and my mom's already
told all her friends about you.

339
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:05,917
Bertie just broke up with me.

340
00:18:07,919 --> 00:18:11,465
-For real? Why?
-I'm sorry, but I--

341
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:13,717
Look, can't you give him
another chance, please?

342
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,427
I mean, this means so much to our family.

343
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,138
Is this because I borrowed money from you?

344
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:20,516
What the hell are you doing?
You should only borrow money from family.

345
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,226
Okay, how much?

346
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:25,312
I mean, I got, like, 60 bucks on me,
but I'm happy to run to an ATM.

347
00:18:25,396 --> 00:18:27,689
-No problem.
-Dude, I'm not an invalid.

348
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,316
You are breaking Mom's heart.

349
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,526
-Me?
-I am?

350
00:18:30,609 --> 00:18:33,028
-Both of you!
-Okay, well, um...

351
00:18:33,111 --> 00:18:34,363
I'm sorry, but I'm gonna go.

352
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:37,949
No, please don't go, okay? Just...
Let's work this out.

353
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,161
There's a lot of great stuff
that you still don't know.

354
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:42,996
[stammers] Little kids love me, right?

355
00:18:43,079 --> 00:18:45,166
And... I can pick up really heavy stuff.

356
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,668
Oh, stop it, dude.
You're humiliating yourself.

357
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:50,421
Listen, one summer,
I got all my mom's old jeans

358
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:52,214
and donated them
to this women's shelter...

359
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:54,049
-Shut up.
-and people thought I was a hero.

360
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:56,092
-You shut up!
-Nobody thought you were a hero!

361
00:18:56,177 --> 00:18:57,511
-Yes, they did, Devon.
-Shut up!

362
00:18:57,594 --> 00:18:59,138
-[Randy] Shut up!
-I wish you the best. Sorry. Bye.

363
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:01,348
-[Randy] Don't leave!
-[Devon] Oh, my God. Don't go.

364
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:03,725
[Jack] The plan was
to wait for Commander--

365
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,436
[Brad] Screw the plan.

366
00:19:05,519 --> 00:19:07,438
We're two clicks away
from a downed jet airliner

367
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:11,024
carrying the president's daughter.
The feds are gonna be all over us.

368
00:19:11,107 --> 00:19:13,694
[Jack] Commander said
he wanted us to wait right here.

369
00:19:13,777 --> 00:19:15,737
Commander ain't here, Jack.

370
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:17,823
The commander ain't here!

371
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,450
-Cut! Cut!
-[Brad] How was that?

372
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:22,118
-Was that... better?
-[Gus sighing]

373
00:19:22,203 --> 00:19:23,329
-Hey.
-Hey.

374
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:24,455
-Morning.
-Morning.

375
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:28,250
-Do you know when the next break is?
-Why? Do you wanna talk to Victor?

376
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:30,836
Yeah. I just...

377
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:34,881
I wanted to let him know why I think
I should be a part of this Arctic movie.

378
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,800
-I just need, like, five minutes.
-Gus, dude...

379
00:19:36,883 --> 00:19:40,011
-I think I can convince him, you know?
-Look, you need to move on, okay?

380
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:41,722
He doesn't need you anymore.

381
00:19:41,805 --> 00:19:44,600
We bought the rights
to the article you mentioned, so...

382
00:19:47,478 --> 00:19:50,314
Wait... What? Are you serious?

383
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:52,483
[softly] Hey, can you keep it down?
We're shooting.

384
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:55,360
You wouldn't have known about that article
unless I had told you about it.

385
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,571
Maybe next time,
you should be more business savvy.

386
00:19:57,654 --> 00:20:00,949
[softly] Business savvy?
This isn't about business, man.

387
00:20:01,032 --> 00:20:03,910
-This is about your feelings towards me.
-We're in the middle of a scene.

388
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:05,746
You didn't like me from the start.

389
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:09,791
What are you talking about?
I... I didn't even know you, okay?

390
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,336
And then you come along,
kissing his ass...

391
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:13,879
I kiss his ass? You kiss his ass.

392
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:16,298
-No, I don't.
-This is his ass. These are your lips.

393
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,633
-Yeah--
-And I'm, like, here.

394
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:18,884
No. No, you're...

395
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,638
This is me. You're, like...
like, on top of me.

396
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:25,932
-[Gus and Tommy continue arguing]
-Hey, hey, hey.

397
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:29,311
-Are you fucking kidding me?
-Pause, pause, pause.

398
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:33,440
-[man] Still rolling! Resetting!
-I'm... I'm sorry. I just...

399
00:20:33,524 --> 00:20:35,567
-I didn't mean to--
-[speaking Korean]

400
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,528
Yeah, he wants you to leave the set.

401
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:39,780
Yeah, like I can trust
anything you translate.

402
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:42,241
-[speaking Korean]
-Forever.

403
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:46,828
[softly] Forever. Go forever.

404
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:52,000
-He said, "Go forever."
-I heard. I know.

405
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:54,670
-[man] Still rolling!
-[Victor] I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

406
00:20:55,211 --> 00:20:56,838
[man] Quiet! Resetting!

407
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:58,465
[organ playing]

408
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:40,341
[clicking]

409
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,638
-Fucking shit.
-[continues clicking lighter]

410
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:07,283
[Dustin] Almost there.
It's just a little farther up.

411
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:09,453
[Wade] I just don't think
snakes are that scary, man.

412
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:12,623
[Dean] Well, my cousin saw one once.
Not here, but he saw... Hey.

413
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:13,749
-Hey.
-Hi.

414
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:15,667
Hey.

415
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:20,255
-You know those guys?
-Uh, friends of a friend.

416
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:23,133
-Where we going?
-Right here. [sighs]

417
00:22:23,216 --> 00:22:24,926
This was Buster's favorite spot.

418
00:22:26,387 --> 00:22:27,596
[sighs]

419
00:22:34,310 --> 00:22:36,062
[indistinct chatter]

420
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:45,238
[man] So there I am, once again,

421
00:22:45,321 --> 00:22:49,868
driving my mother home
because she's too wasted to drive.

422
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:54,206
And, um, I'm just about to tell her
how fucking sick of this I am.

423
00:22:54,706 --> 00:23:01,004
And then I stop
and remind myself of, uh, the don'ts.

424
00:23:01,087 --> 00:23:06,968
Don't nag, scold or complain.
Don't push anyone but yourself.

425
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:10,806
Don't, uh... don't keep checking up
on the alcoholic.

426
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:14,059
Don't be overprotective.

427
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:17,312
And when I got to the end of that list,

428
00:23:18,564 --> 00:23:21,942
I was able to let go of the anger...

429
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,695
and just love my mom.

430
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:30,701
[both breathing heavily]

431
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:38,792
I can't keep checking up on her.

432
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:42,463
Sometimes that's the hardest part.

433
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:46,007
I have to remember
that the best thing I can do...

434
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:50,262
is let go of all the things
that I can't change

435
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:55,016
and start thinking
about the things that I can.

436
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,810
[breathing heavily]

437
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:02,148
[Gus] I've been seeing this girl.

438
00:24:02,232 --> 00:24:05,819
We've been dating, and she's an alcoholic.

439
00:24:05,902 --> 00:24:11,324
And... lately I've been feeling her,
like, pulling away from me.

440
00:24:14,077 --> 00:24:15,245
Now I get it.

441
00:24:17,998 --> 00:24:19,082
I get it.

442
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:24,713
I've just been, like, putting...
[inhales deeply]

443
00:24:24,796 --> 00:24:28,258
so much pressure on her to get better.

444
00:24:31,177 --> 00:24:33,054
So I'm gonna take a step back...

445
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:37,893
let her handle her own recovery,
and, um...

446
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:41,479
maybe if I do that...

447
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:47,068
we'll have something real.

448
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:57,579
-[Mickey] Hey there.
-Hi.

449
00:24:57,663 --> 00:24:59,455
-How'd it go with Randy?
-Oh...

450
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:01,708
It was worse than I could have imagined.

451
00:25:01,792 --> 00:25:03,710
It was a little bit
like watching a horror movie

452
00:25:03,794 --> 00:25:05,754
and being in the horror movie as well.

453
00:25:05,837 --> 00:25:09,424
-And you're already on Tinder.
-Oh, yeah. I'm liking everyone.

454
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:12,093
Uh, what does it mean when someone says
they're a project manager?

455
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,637
They're unemployed.

456
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:16,222
If it says project manager or CEO,
they're unemployed.

457
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:18,433
Oh, okay. Well,
they're still getting a like from me.

458
00:25:18,516 --> 00:25:20,602
Don't do that! They're all gonna text you.

459
00:25:20,686 --> 00:25:22,228
That's good. It'll make me feel popular.

460
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:24,397
I've only got, like,
seven people in my phone.

461
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:26,524
-[knocking on door]
-I'll get it.

462
00:25:30,528 --> 00:25:32,322
-[Dustin] Hey.
-[Mickey] Hi.

463
00:25:32,405 --> 00:25:34,157
-Spontaneous drop-by.
-Yeah.

464
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:36,409
I was in the neighborhood,
grabbed some artichokes.

465
00:25:36,492 --> 00:25:38,579
These things are so expensive,
they should come with a handjob.

466
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:40,246
-[chuckles]
-Uh, hi.

467
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:41,164
Hello.

468
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:45,001
Oh, sorry. Uh, Bertie, this is Dustin,
an old friend of mine.

469
00:25:45,085 --> 00:25:47,503
And Dustin, this is Bertie, my roommate.

470
00:25:47,588 --> 00:25:50,256
-Roommate and future old friend.
-[Mickey chuckles]

471
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,843
You, uh, hungry? I'll cook these up.

472
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:55,553
-Oh, wow. That's so nice of you.
-Happy to help.

473
00:25:56,471 --> 00:25:58,556
Oh, my God. This is your kitchen?

474
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:00,767
Maybe this was a mistake.

475
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:02,310
[Mickey and Dustin chuckle]

476
00:26:03,228 --> 00:26:05,480
So how do you two know each other?

477
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:08,650
-Mmm... Mickey and I used to date.
-[Bertie] Oh.

478
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:10,360
